- **The generator acts on some of the properties.** `GenerationMode`, `WriteIndented`, `OmitXmlDeclaration`, `DefaultNamespace`, `PropertyNamingPolicy`, `ElementNamingPolicy`, `AttributeNamingPolicy`, `IncludeFields`, `DefaultIgnoreCondition`, `DefaultPropertyMapping`, `PreferredObjectCreationHandling`, `RespectNullableAnnotations`, and `UnknownTypeHandling` take effect.
- **The other properties aren't copied to the options.** Setting `DiscriminatorPlacement`, `EnumHandling`, `EmitByteOrderMark`, `IgnoreReadOnlyFields`, `IgnoreReadOnlyProperties`, `MaxDepth`, `PropertyNameCaseInsensitive`, `UseStringEnumConverter`, or `XmlVersion` leaves the options of `Default` at their defaults. To use those settings, pass an `XmlSerializerOptions` instance to the constructor of the context.
- **The write fast path is compiled for the attribute's values.** The naming policies, `DefaultPropertyMapping`, and `IncludeFields` fix the names and the choice of members in the write fast path. When you pass options to the constructor that differ in one of them, the fast path isn't used: a context in the default mode writes from the metadata and follows your options.
- **Indented output uses `Environment.NewLine`.** The attribute has no `NewLine` property. Pass options to the constructor to choose the line ending.
